      "message": "First because we can implement it after this fix which gets rid of the runtime crashes entirely.\n\nSecond because, I don\u0027t like \"optimistic\" algorithms which can widely alter the timing of `gn gen` times. This will increase its variance, leading to surprising results when benchmarking. Results may change due to a kernel upgrade, or be widely inconsistent between different OSes.\n\nAlso, ideally, I want to get rid of the validations-collecting walks in the Fuchsia build entirely so this wouldn\u0027t be needed at all.\n\nSo I don\u0027t think it\u0027s really worth it, but it can be implemented.\n\nBesides, I have other optimizations to speed up metadata collection deterministically that I intend to push soon, if you\u0027re interested in that.",
